# Public API routes and reverse proxy

When you add or change a **root-level** Nest `@Controller('…')` (paths like `/first-reactions/...`, not nested under `/accounts/:id/...`):

## Checklist (all three)

1. **Production nginx** — add a `location` block in `deploy/nginx/snippets/app-proxy.conf`:
   ```nginx
   location /<prefix>/ {
       proxy_pass http://api;
       include /etc/nginx/snippets/proxy-api.conf;
   }
   ```
   If the repo still mirrors locations in `deploy/nginx/nginx.https.conf.example`, add the same block there.

2. **Local dev** — add the same prefix to `app/vite.config.ts` → `server.proxy` (target `http://localhost:3000`).

3. **Docs** — one line in `docs/deploy-vps.md` § «Публичные API-префиксы» if this is a new module.

## Do not confuse with SPA routes

- OBS/dashboard pages under `/modules/.../widget/...` are served by `location /` → `index.html`. **No** extra nginx `location` for those.
- Only **browser `fetch()` to the API host** needs the proxy prefix (e.g. `GET /first-reactions/widget/:ucid`).

## Existing prefixes (keep in sync when auditing)

`/auth/`, `/accounts/`, `/join/`, `/bonus-buys/`, `/prize-spins/`, `/chat-rolls/`, `/media-interactive/`, `/first-reactions/`, `/webhooks/`, `/internal/`

Routes under `/accounts/` are already covered by `location /accounts/`.
